Contains PrismML Bonsai transforms and packed ternary kernels from
https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp (MIT).
The included qvac-bonsai-v2.patch ports the tied-embedding/output Hadamard v2
contract from Prism revision 11809184898113482c2f510fd13da669aaba1052,
src/llama-model.cpp and src/llama-model.h. The unmodified QVAC pin rejects
the published model's Hadamard version 2. The patch retains QVAC's backend
allocation and graph implementation, adding Prism's validation and binding.

AntiSocial's additional runtime patches are qvac-android-vulkan-dispatch.patch
(instance-dispatched Vulkan 1.1 queries for stock Android API 26/27 loaders),
qvac-pq2-ssse3.patch (exact packed CPU dot product on the Android x86_64
SSSE3 baseline), and qvac-bounded-shader-build.patch (build scheduling only).
The SSSE3 path is compared with QVAC's independent scalar decoder over 5,000
randomized coefficient/scale cases by kernel_reference.cpp.

The Bonsai 2 model files are separately published by PrismML under Apache 2.0.
Model weights are optional downloaded data and are never bundled in this code.
Selected runtime/backend support is reported separately from phone qualification.

qvac-online-kv-v2.patch adds AntiSocial's protected online cache, direct mixed
attention, immutable recipe state and independently implemented cache rotations.
Planar/Iso mathematics was researched from RotorQuant and compared with the MIT
llama-cpp-turboquant donor at 08e025c06ab521e4fa9e5c08b80af57614543e53:
https://github.com/johndpope/llama-cpp-turboquant
https://github.com/scrya-com/rotorquant/tree/fcd76768650659cad2f40a45a330612a7af8f928
No unlicensed RotorQuant implementation source is redistributed by this patch.
